<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mat Salleh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1900</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Datu Muhammad Salleh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mat Salleh, or Datu Muhammad Salleh, was a chief of Bajau and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suluk">Suluk</a> descent from the Sugut river region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a> who led a rebellion against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-north-borneo-company">British North Borneo Company</a> from 1894. His followers burned the company's settlement on Gaya Island in 1897. After a short peace with the company he resumed fighting and was killed in January 1900 at his fort at Tambunan. He is remembered in Malaysia as a hero of resistance.</p></div>
